      source: "Line engraving of Joseph Fourier by Amedee-Felix-Barthelemy Geille after a drawing by J. Boilly, lettered 'J. Boilly Del.', 'Geille Sculp.' and 'J. FOURIER.'; Wellcome Collection, London (work b4qh352u). The museum scan (2188 x 3328 pixels) was cropped to the plate and its caption and downscaled once to 739 x 1200 pixels; nothing was upscaled. Shown as a later engraving after another artist's likeness, not as a documented sitting.",
