      proactive_agency: [68, 0.55, "s", "A"],
      // [src_equiano_nge, src_equiano_slavery, src_equiano_narrative | 1760s | encyclopedia entry, institutional biography, his own text] While enslaved he bought goods and traded them on his own account on voyages around the Caribbean and Savannah River, as the encyclopedia and the Slavery and Remembrance biography describe, and later built a living as a hairdresser, steward and author (his own text); the Narrative gives the detail of the ventures, the two institutional texts only summarise them, and the Narrative is a self-report whose early chapters are disputed.
      resourcefulness: [66, 0.5, "s", "A"],
      // [src_equiano_nge, src_equiano_slavery, src_equiano_narrative | 1760s-1766 | encyclopedia entry, institutional biography, his own text] Working toward buying his freedom through trading over several years until he bought it on Montserrat in 1766 is stated by two institutional texts and told in detail in his own Narrative; the institutional texts repeat the Narrative's account rather than independent records, so the evidence is largely self-report. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): top-risk row; lowered from 68 / 0.55 to 64 / 0.50 because the multi-year saving episode rests on his own Narrative, which Carretta's documentary challenge (nativity source) shows he shaped for his readers.
      persistence: [64, 0.5, "s", "A"],
      // [src_equiano_ew_irwin, src_equiano_ew_sierra, src_equiano_nge | 1787 | reference site, reference site, encyclopedia entry] As commissary he complained to the Navy Commissioners and to Captain Thompson about Irwin's failure to supply contracted goods and was relieved of his post after the Committee sided with Irwin; Thompson wrote that the quarrel between the two men was disrupting the voyage and Irwin said Vassa was arrogant to white people. The complaint is documented, but the supply allegations are his own and Thompson blamed both men. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): top-risk row; lowered from 64 / 0.48 to 60 / 0.42 because the substance of the allegations is Vassa's own, an independent captain blamed both parties, and the reference site cites no footnotes.
      conflict_tolerance: [60, 0.42, "s", "D"],
      // [src_equiano_nge, src_equiano_encyc, src_equiano_slavery | 1766-1789 | encyclopedia entry, reference entry, institutional biography] After 1766 he worked as a sailor and steward on Mediterranean, Atlantic and Arctic voyages (the 1773 Phipps expedition), went to the Mosquito Coast, worked as a hairdresser and commissary and became an author, according to the sources, which list the moves without describing how he handled any of them; the breadth is documented but the quality of the adaptation is not.
      adaptability: [62, 0.45, "s", "A"],
