      source: "Photograph of Tsuda Umeko captioned in print 'Tsuda Umeko joshi' (Ms Tsuda Umeko), the first portrait on the National Diet Library's Portraits of Modern Japanese Historical Figures page for her, taken from Yoshikawa Toshikazu, 'Tsuda Umeko' (Tokyo: Fujo Shimbunsha, 1930; NDL Digital Collections item 1191056). The photographer and the date of the sitting are not given in the book. The file is the NDL's unmodified image (733 x 1117 px), including the printed caption strip; no upscaling or cropping.",
